{
  "about": [
    "What counts as a finished part of a form, written down once.",
    "",
    "The rules exist twice over: in Java, where they decide whether a form is finished and goes to the",
    "advisor to be signed, and in the browser, where they tick the rail as somebody types. Neither can be",
    "deleted \u2014 one is authoritative, the other is live \u2014 so this file is what stops them disagreeing. Both",
    "sides run these answers through their own rules and have to arrive at the same verdicts.",
    "",
    "A case is a set of answers, the lines a document has been attached for, and what each part should then",
    "come to. Add a case whenever a rule is written or changed, and change it in this file first: it is the",
    "specification, and the two implementations are what have to follow it.",
    "",
    "Kept in both repositories, synced rather than shared, because they are two repositories. Within either,",
    "a rule that drifts from this file fails the build."
  ],
